(window.IND_GITA_V = window.IND_GITA_V || {})[15] = [{"v":1,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"ऊर्ध्वमूलमधःशाखमश्वत्थं प्राहुरव्ययम् ।\nछन्दांसि यस्य पर्णानि यस्तं वेद स वेदवित् ॥","iast":"ūrdhvamūlamadhaḥśākhamaśvatthaṃ prāhuravyayam |\nchandāṃsi yasya parṇāni yastaṃ veda sa vedavit ||","read":"oordhvamoolamadhahshaakhamashvattham praahuravyayam |\nchhandaamsi yasya parnaani yastam veda sa vedavit ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: With roots above, branches below, the Asvattha is said to be indestructible; the leaves of it are hymns; he who knoweth it is a Veda-knower.","en2":"They speak of an eternal Ashvattha rooted above and branching below, whose leaves are the Vedas; he who knows it, is a Veda-knower.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":2,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अधश्चोर्ध्वं प्रसृतास्तस्य शाखा गुणप्रवृद्धा विषयप्रवालाः ।\nअधश्च मूलान्यनुसन्ततानि कर्मानुबन्धीनि मनुष्यलोके ॥","iast":"adhaścordhvaṃ prasṛtāstasya śākhā guṇapravṛddhā viṣayapravālāḥ |\nadhaśca mūlānyanusantatāni karmānubandhīni manuṣyaloke ||","read":"adhashchordhvam prasritaastasya shaakhaa gunapravriddhaa vishayapravaalaah |\nadhashcha moolaanyanusantataani karmaanubandheeni manushyaloke ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Downwards and upwards spread the branches of it, nourished by the qualities; the objects of the senses its buds; and its roots grow downwards, the bonds of action in the world of men.","en2":"Below and above spread its branches, nourished by the Gunas; sense-objects are its buds; and below in the world of man stretch forth the roots, originating action.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":3,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न रूपमस्येह तथोपलभ्यते नान्तो न चादिर्न च संप्रतिष्ठा ।\nअश्वत्थमेनं सुविरूढमूल मसङ्गशस्त्रेण दृढेन छित्त्वा ॥","iast":"na rūpamasyeha tathopalabhyate nānto na cādirna ca saṃpratiṣṭhā |\naśvatthamenaṃ suvirūḍhamūla masaṅgaśastreṇa dṛḍhena chittvā ||","read":"na roopamasyeha tathopalabhyate naanto na chaadirna cha sampratishthaa |\nashvatthamenam suviroodhamoola masangashastrena dridhena chhittvaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Nor here may be acquired knowledge of its form, nor its end, nor its origin, nor its rooting-place; this strongly rooted Asvattha having been cut down by the unswerving weapon of non-attachment,","en2":"Its form is not here perceived as such, neither its end, nor its origin, nor its existence. Having cut asunder this firm-rooted Ashvattha with the strong axe of non-attachment,—then that Goal is to be sought for, going whither they (the wise) do not return again. I seek refuge in that Primeval Purusha whence streamed forth the Eternal Activity.","en2r":"15.3-4","rv":null},{"v":4,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ततः पदं तत्परिमार्गितव्यं यस्मिन्गता न निवर्तन्ति भूयः ।\nतमेव चाद्यं पुरुषं प्रपद्ये यतः प्रवृत्तिः प्रसृता पुराणी ॥","iast":"tataḥ padaṃ tatparimārgitavyaṃ yasmingatā na nivartanti bhūyaḥ |\ntameva cādyaṃ puruṣaṃ prapadye yataḥ pravṛttiḥ prasṛtā purāṇī ||","read":"tatah padam tatparimaargitavyam yasmingataa na nivartanti bhooyah |\ntameva chaadyam purusham prapadye yatah pravrittih prasritaa puraanee ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That path beyond may be sought, treading which there is no return. I go indeed to that Primal Man, whence the ancient energy forth-streamed.","en2":"Its form is not here perceived as such, neither its end, nor its origin, nor its existence. Having cut asunder this firm-rooted Ashvattha with the strong axe of non-attachment,—then that Goal is to be sought for, going whither they (the wise) do not return again. I seek refuge in that Primeval Purusha whence streamed forth the Eternal Activity.","en2r":"15.3-4","rv":null},{"v":5,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"निर्मानमोहा जितसङ्गदोषा अध्यात्मनित्या विनिवृत्तकामाः ।\nद्वन्द्वैर्विमुक्ताः सुखदुःखसंज्ञै र्गच्छन्त्यमूढाः पदमव्ययं तत् ॥","iast":"nirmānamohā jitasaṅgadoṣā adhyātmanityā vinivṛttakāmāḥ |\ndvandvairvimuktāḥ sukhaduḥkhasaṃjñai rgacchantyamūḍhāḥ padamavyayaṃ tat ||","read":"nirmaanamohaa jitasangadoshaa adhyaatmanityaa vinivrittakaamaah |\ndvandvairvimuktaah sukhaduhkhasamjnai rgachchhantyamoodhaah padamavyayam tat ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Without pride and delusion, victorious over the vice of attachment, dwelling constantly in the Self, desire pacified, liberated from the pairs of opposites known as pleasure and pain, they tread, undeluded, that indestructible path.","en2":"Free from pride and delusion, with the evil of attachment conquered, ever dwelling in the Self, with desires completely receded, liberated from the pairs of opposites known as pleasure and pain, the undeluded reach that Goal Eternal.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":6,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न तद्भासयते सूर्यो न शशाङ्को न पावकः ।\nयद्गत्वा न निवर्तन्ते तद्धाम परमं मम ॥","iast":"na tadbhāsayate sūryo na śaśāṅko na pāvakaḥ |\nyadgatvā na nivartante taddhāma paramaṃ mama ||","read":"na tadbhaasayate sooryo na shashaanko na paavakah |\nyadgatvaa na nivartante taddhaama paramam mama ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Nor doth the sun lighten there, nor moon, nor fire; having gone thither they return not; that is My supreme abode.","en2":"That the sun illumines not, nor the moon, nor fire; that is My Supreme Abode, going whither they return not.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":7,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ममैवांशो जीवलोके जीवभूतः सनातनः ।\nमनःषष्ठानीन्द्रियाणि प्रकृतिस्थानि कर्षति ॥","iast":"mamaivāṃśo jīvaloke jīvabhūtaḥ sanātanaḥ |\nmanaḥṣaṣṭhānīndriyāṇi prakṛtisthāni karṣati ||","read":"mamaivaamsho jeevaloke jeevabhootah sanaatanah |\nmanahshashthaaneendriyaani prakritisthaani karshati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"A portion of Mine own Self, transformed in the world of life into an immortal Spirit, draweth round itself the senses of which the mind is the sixth, veiled in matter.","en2":"An eternal portion of Myself having become a living soul in the world of life, draws (to itself) the (five) senses with mind for the sixth, abiding in Prakriti.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":8,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"शरीरं यदवाप्नोति यच्चाप्युत्क्रामतीश्वरः ।\nगृहीत्वैतानि संयाति वायुर्गन्धानिवाशयात् ॥","iast":"śarīraṃ yadavāpnoti yaccāpyutkrāmatīśvaraḥ |\ngṛhītvaitāni saṃyāti vāyurgandhānivāśayāt ||","read":"shareeram yadavaapnoti yachchaapyutkraamateeshvarah |\ngriheetvaitaani samyaati vaayurgandhaanivaashayaat ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"When the Lord acquireth a body and when He abandoneth it, He seizeth these and goeth with them, as the wind takes fragrances from their retreats","en2":"When the Lord obtains a body and when He leaves it, He takes these and goes, as the wind takes the scents from their seats (the flowers).","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":9,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"श्रोत्रं चक्षुः स्पर्शनं च रसनं घ्राणमेव च ।\nअधिष्ठाय मनश्चायं विषयानुपसेवते ॥","iast":"śrotraṃ cakṣuḥ sparśanaṃ ca rasanaṃ ghrāṇameva ca |\nadhiṣṭhāya manaścāyaṃ viṣayānupasevate ||","read":"shrotram chakshuh sparshanam cha rasanam ghraanameva cha |\nadhishthaaya manashchaayam vishayaanupasevate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Enshrined in the ear, the eye, the touch, the taste and the smell, and in the mind also, He enjoyeth the objects of the senses","en2":"Presiding over the ear, the eye, the touch, the taste and the smell, as also the mind, He experiences objects.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":10,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"उत्क्रामन्तं स्थितं वापि भुञ्जानं वा गुणान्वितम् ।\nविमूढा नानुपश्यन्ति पश्यन्ति ज्ञानचक्षुषः ॥","iast":"utkrāmantaṃ sthitaṃ vāpi bhuñjānaṃ vā guṇānvitam |\nvimūḍhā nānupaśyanti paśyanti jñānacakṣuṣaḥ ||","read":"utkraamantam sthitam vaapi bhunjaanam vaa gunaanvitam |\nvimoodhaa naanupashyanti pashyanti jnaanachakshushah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The deluded do not perceive (Him) when He departeth or stayeth or enjoyeth, swayed by the qualities; the wisdom-eyed perceive.","en2":"Him while transmigrating from one body to another, or residing (in the same) or experiencing, or when united with the Gunas,—the deluded do not see; but those who have the eye of wisdom behold Him.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":11,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यतन्तो योगिनश्चैनं पश्यन्त्यात्मन्यवस्थितम् ।\nयतन्तोऽप्यकृतात्मानो नैनं पश्यन्त्यचेतसः ॥","iast":"yatanto yoginaścainaṃ paśyantyātmanyavasthitam |\nyatanto’pyakṛtātmāno nainaṃ paśyantyacetasaḥ ||","read":"yatanto yoginashchainam pashyantyaatmanyavasthitam |\nyatanto'pyakritaatmaano nainam pashyantyachetasah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Yogîs also, struggling, perceive Him, established in the Self; but though struggling, the unintelligent perceive Him not, their selves untrained.","en2":"The Yogis striving (for perfection) behold Him dwelling in themselves; but the unrefined and unintelligent, even though striving, see Him not.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":12,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यदादित्यगतं तेजो जगद्भासयतेऽखिलम् ।\nयच्चन्द्रमसि यच्चाग्नौ तत्तेजो विद्धि मामकम् ॥","iast":"yadādityagataṃ tejo jagadbhāsayate’khilam |\nyaccandramasi yaccāgnau tattejo viddhi māmakam ||","read":"yadaadityagatam tejo jagadbhaasayate'khilam |\nyachchandramasi yachchaagnau tattejo viddhi maamakam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That splendour issuing from the sun that enlighteneth the whole world, that which is in the moon and in fire, that splendour know as from Me.","en2":"The light which, residing in the sun illumines the whole world, that which is in the moon and in the fire—know that light to be Mine.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":13,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"गामाविश्य च भूतानि धारयाम्यहमोजसा ।\nपुष्णामि चौषधीः सर्वाः सोमो भूत्वा रसात्मकः ॥","iast":"gāmāviśya ca bhūtāni dhārayāmyahamojasā |\npuṣṇāmi cauṣadhīḥ sarvāḥ somo bhūtvā rasātmakaḥ ||","read":"gaamaavishya cha bhootaani dhaarayaamyahamojasaa |\npushnaami chaushadheeh sarvaah somo bhootvaa rasaatmakah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Permeating the soil, I support beings by my vital energy, and having become the delicious Soma I nourish all plants.","en2":"Entering the earth with My energy, I support all beings, and I nourish all the herbs, becoming the watery moon.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":14,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अहं वैश्वानरो भूत्वा प्राणिनां देहमाश्रितः ।\nप्राणापानसमायुक्तः पचाम्यन्नं चतुर्विधम् ॥","iast":"ahaṃ vaiśvānaro bhūtvā prāṇināṃ dehamāśritaḥ |\nprāṇāpānasamāyuktaḥ pacāmyannaṃ caturvidham ||","read":"aham vaishvaanaro bhootvaa praaninaam dehamaashritah |\npraanaapaanasamaayuktah pachaamyannam chaturvidham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"I, having become the Fire of Life, take possession of the bodies of breathing things, and united with the life-breaths, I digest the four kinds of food.","en2":"Abiding in the body of living beings as (the fire) Vaishvânara, I, associated with Prâna and Apâna, digest the fourfold food.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":15,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सर्वस्य चाहं हृदि सन्निविष्टो मत्तः स्मृतिर्ज्ञानमपोहनं च ।\nवेदैश्च सर्वैरहमेव वेद्यो वेदान्तकृद्वेदविदेव चाहम् ॥","iast":"sarvasya cāhaṃ hṛdi sanniviṣṭo mattaḥ smṛtirjñānamapohanaṃ ca |\nvedaiśca sarvairahameva vedyo vedāntakṛdvedavideva cāham ||","read":"sarvasya chaaham hridi sannivishto mattah smritirjnaanamapohanam cha |\nvedaishcha sarvairahameva vedyo vedaantakridvedavideva chaaham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"And I am seated in the hearts of all, and from Me memory and wisdom and their absence. And that which is to be known in all the Vedas am I; and I indeed the Veda-knower and the author of the Vedanta.","en2":"I am centred in the hearts of all; memory and perception as well as their loss come from Me. I am verily that which has to be known by all the Vedas, I indeed am the Author of the Vedânta, and the Knower of the Veda am I.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":16,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"द्वाविमौ पुरुषौ लोके क्षरश्चाक्षर एव च ।\nक्षरः सर्वाणि भूतानि कूटस्थोऽक्षर उच्यते ॥","iast":"dvāvimau puruṣau loke kṣaraścākṣara eva ca |\nkṣaraḥ sarvāṇi bhūtāni kūṭastho’kṣara ucyate ||","read":"dvaavimau purushau loke ksharashchaakshara eva cha |\nksharah sarvaani bhootaani kootastho'kshara uchyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"There are two Energies in this world, the destructible and the indestructible; the destructible is all beings, the unchanging is called the indestructible.","en2":"There are two Purushas in the world,—the Perishable and the Imperishable. All beings are the Perishable; and the Kutastha is called Imperishable.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":17,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"उत्तमः पुरुषस्त्वन्यः परमात्मेत्युदाहृतः ।\nयो लोकत्रयमाविश्य बिभर्त्यव्यय ईश्वरः ॥","iast":"uttamaḥ puruṣastvanyaḥ paramātmetyudāhṛtaḥ |\nyo lokatrayamāviśya bibhartyavyaya īśvaraḥ ||","read":"uttamah purushastvanyah paramaatmetyudaahritah |\nyo lokatrayamaavishya bibhartyavyaya eeshvarah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The highest Energy is verily Another, declared as the Supreme Self, He who, pervading all, sustaineth the three worlds, the indestructible Lord.","en2":"But (there is) another, the Supreme Purusha, called the Highest Self, the immutable Lord, who pervading the three worlds, sustains them.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":18,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यस्मात्क्षरमतीतोऽहमक्षरादपि चोत्तमः ।\nअतोऽस्मि लोके वेदे च प्रथितः पुरुषोत्तमः ॥","iast":"yasmātkṣaramatīto’hamakṣarādapi cottamaḥ |\nato’smi loke vede ca prathitaḥ puruṣottamaḥ ||","read":"yasmaatksharamateeto'hamaksharaadapi chottamah |\nato'smi loke vede cha prathitah purushottamah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Since I excel the destructible, and am more excellent also than the indestructible, in the world and in the Veda I am proclaimed the Supreme Spirit.","en2":"As I transcend the Perishable and am above even the Imperishable, therefore am I in the world and in the Veda celebrated as the Purushottama, (the Highest Purusha).","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":19,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यो मामेवमसम्मूढो जानाति पुरुषोत्तमम् ।\nस सर्वविद्भजति मां सर्वभावेन भारत ॥","iast":"yo māmevamasammūḍho jānāti puruṣottamam |\nsa sarvavidbhajati māṃ sarvabhāvena bhārata ||","read":"yo maamevamasammoodho jaanaati purushottamam |\nsa sarvavidbhajati maam sarvabhaavena bhaarata ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who undeluded knoweth Me thus as the Supreme Spirit, he, all-knowing, worshippeth Me with his whole being, O Bhârata.","en2":"He who free from delusion thus knows Me, the Highest Spirit, he knowing all, worships Me with all his heart, O descendant of Bharata.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":20,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"इति गुह्यतमं शास्त्रमिदमुक्तं मयाऽनघ ।\nएतद्बुद्ध्वा बुद्धिमान्स्यात्कृतकृत्यश्च भारत ॥","iast":"iti guhyatamaṃ śāstramidamuktaṃ mayā’nagha |\netadbuddhvā buddhimānsyātkṛtakṛtyaśca bhārata ||","read":"iti guhyatamam shaastramidamuktam mayaa'nagha |\netadbuddhvaa buddhimaansyaatkritakrityashcha bhaarata ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Thus by Me this most secret teaching hath been told O sinless one. This known, he hath become illuminated and hath finished his work, O Bhârata.","en2":"Thus, O sinless one, has this most profound teaching been imparted by Me. Knowing this one attains the highest intelligence and will have accomplished all one's duties, O descendant of Bharata.","en2r":null,"rv":null}];
